TestEvaluationPrograms:
    Run the five example programs through the real executable test command.
    Require every program to complete its assertions successfully.

TestUnknownMessagesPropagateAndHandlersRemainUsable:
    Send missing selectors to primitives, collections, blocks, native objects,
    builtin services, workspace and coordinator through MCP.
    Require immediate tool errors that name the selector and skip later code.
    Check missing-variable arithmetic and missing super sends also signal.
    Preserve explicit/inherited doesNotUnderstand handlers and onError recovery.

TestNumericDivisionFailuresAndModuloSyntax:
    Require zero divisors and wrong divisor kinds to signal before later effects.
    Check ordinary and reflective modulo syntax and catchable numeric errors.
    Verify empty string results stay empty through MCP, while nil still prints nil.

TestComparatorReadsAndFailuresKeepArrayUsable:
    Sort while a comparator reads the receiver; require no deadlock.
    Signal from a comparator and require the original ordering to remain editable.
    Mutate from a comparator and reject the sorted commit without losing mutations.
    Check a bound Array workspace supports implicit size and isolated missing vars.

TestScriptRejectsMissingMessagesAndClasses:
    Run missing-selector, missing-class and succeeding scripts in one batch.
    Require two failures, continued execution and a failing command exit code.
